%erg 0.1
Title: erg-pr-merge: add a -C PATH flag so the bare rule-matched invocation works from any cwd
Created: 2026-07-14
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-07-14T16:40Z claude created
2026-07-14T20:06Z claude note planned by raid — -C parse lands before any git/gh call; skip trigger is the -d tickets clause, not erg resolution

--- body ---
## Context

The standing permission rule `Bash(~/.claude/skills/merge/erg-pr-merge:*)`
(settings.json, committed 2026-07-10) deterministically authorizes merges —
but only for the BARE invocation: the rule prefix-matches the whole command
text, so `cd <worktree> && erg-pr-merge N` starts with `cd` and falls through
to the stochastic auto-mode classifier, which denies self-merges
unpredictably. The 2026-07-14 raid wave (#601-#603) stalled on exactly this
until the bare form was found; it then had to round-trip the PRIMARY checkout
through each PR branch (worktree remove + `git -C` checkout per PR) because
the script is cwd-based and the session's base cwd was a husk. Two further
costs of the workaround: the primary dance is contention-prone under parallel
sessions, and with cwd outside a checkout `erg-pr-merge` found no
`tickets/erg` binary and SKIPPED the ticket close on #601/#602 (chore-close
PR required).

## Relevant files

- `skills/merge/erg-pr-merge` — arg parsing at "Step 0: resolve PR"
- `skills/merge/SKILL.md` — states "cwd-based — it never takes a repo or
  path argument"; must be updated to document -C and the bare-invocation
  permission synergy

## Actions

1. Accept `-C <path>` as the first argument: `cd` there before anything
   else, die loudly if the path is missing or not a directory.
2. Update SKILL.md: document -C, and state that the canonical agent
   invocation is the bare form
   `~/.claude/skills/merge/erg-pr-merge -C WORKTREE N`,
   which matches the standing allow rule from any cwd.
3. Keep backward compatibility: no -C means current behavior, byte-identical.

## Test

- Red-first: invoke erg-pr-merge -C <tmp-worktree> with a stub gh, assert it
  operates on the target checkout (branch check reads the -C repo, not cwd).

## Invariants

- Existing callers without -C are untouched (test_erg_pr_merge suites stay
  green).
- The -C path must land INSIDE the target checkout before any git/gh/erg
  call — no half-cd states.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg-pr-merge -C <path> <N>` merges from an arbitrary cwd
- [ ] SKILL.md documents the flag and the bare-invocation rule synergy
- [ ] Ticket-close step finds tickets/erg via the -C checkout (no more
      skipped closes)
- [ ] `make check` passes
